From: Abbas Rizvi <abbas.rizvi@nomadrail.com>
Subject: [TRIAG-8585] report_dosto_neu.py — Bug 10 (number_coaches BFS infinite
 loop guard)

File: lib/report/report_dosto_neu.py

Bug 10  number_coaches() BFS unconditionally re-enqueues to_device even when no
        branch assigned it a coach_number. APs / edge-of-consist switches with a
        missing or duplicate position get popped, re-walked, re-enqueued forever
        -> `obn report` pegs 100% CPU and leaks 27 GB+ RSS (Fzg 130 2026-05-12,
        Fzg 8 2026-05-22). Only re-enqueue when a coach_number was assigned.
---
--- a/lib/report/report_dosto_neu.py
+++ b/lib/report/report_dosto_neu.py
@@ Bug 10: number_coaches BFS re-enqueue guard @@
                     # nv6 - END

-                # Add to_device to queue
-                queue.appendleft(to_device)
+                # Add to_device to queue # NDP-PATCH-BUG10-BFS-GUARD
+                # Bug 10 fix: only enqueue if coach_number was assigned in
+                # one of the branches above. Without this, APs and edge
+                # switches whose conditions didn't match get re-enqueued
+                # forever, hanging obn report at 100% CPU.
+                if to_device.coach_number is not None:
+                    queue.appendleft(to_device)
                 continue
